  point up areas needing improvement)?
..Are attempts being made to flesh out the unspoken rules of this list (and by 
   extension lists/conversation/social interaction in general)?

  Many thanks to Tim May for your clearheaded discussion on robust and weak
systems. I would like to add that if you rank systems by robustness the
most robust offer the greatest rewards to those who crack them in their
existing form and/or make improvements.

For example:

Laws of nature... require major science/invention to crack..great rewards
Economy... takes effort to come out ahead but well worth it
State rule... at one extreem run a few red lights and don't get caught, at
the other set a new legal precedent
PPL's.....(unless I'm missing something)... no great rewards

Happy New Year


