Subject: Pets or food

Here's a personal anecdote regarding that delicate distinction:

   I spent a month in a Hong Kong hotel at age 8. They served dogmeat and
kept puppies in a glass cage in the dining room. When I figured out what
was happening when the puppies dissappeared I swore I'd never eat meat
again, any meat. 

   The cook sensing my plight asked my parents if I could visit his home on
his day off. My parents reluctantly agreed and I spent the afternoon
playing with his pet pig. He swore the pig was his family pet and would
never be eaten. (I'm not as easily pursuaded now but at 8 I bought the
story.) I believe he was earnestly trying to show me that dogs are food and
pigs are pets. Black dogs were supposed to be especially tasty. Haven't had
the urge for dogburger lately (or for pork either for that matter). 

   Since then I've  perceived "cuteness" as a particularly arbitrary guality.

Bon Apetite!

